From 5a3009954e82b4859c34e1df721d44096fcbe8a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AliGram <aligram@local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/67] chore(aligram): distinct AliGram branding (BRANDING.md)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

applicationId nu.gpu.nagram -> app.aligram (gradle.properties);
hardcoded package refs in the manifest mime types, auth.xml,
auth_menu.xml, contacts.xml, sync_contacts.xml updated to
app.aligram. App name 'Nagram X' -> 'AliGram' in AppName / NagramX
strings (base + all locales) and in the app-name sentences
(UnifiedPush, CustomTitleHint, PushServiceTypeInApp, NekoSettings).
Original AliGram icon (teal rounded square + white paper plane,
drawn from scratch with PIL; no Nagram art copied) in all mipmap
densities + round variants + adaptive-icon XMLs + 512px playstore
asset; application icon/roundIcon and the sole remaining launcher
alias (DefaultIcon, enabled=true) point at it. The 14 Nagram
icon-variant activity-aliases were deleted from the manifest and
LauncherIconController reduced to the single DEFAULT entry.
QRCodeWriter / BlockingUpdateView and the notification-icon option 1
use the new icon (white plane aligram_notification).
Crashlytics stays disabled: shouldEnableCrashlytics() now returns
false (the upstream Firebase project in google-services.json belongs
to Nagram and is left untouched — push will not work for the new id
until AliGram has its own Firebase project).
Residual (documented): the unreferenced Nagram PNG assets remain in
the tree; google-services.json is untouched; the legacy 'Nagram'
notification-icon variant (option 2) and the upstream channel links
in About remain.
